  "plain": "In experiments from 2024, a parent looks at a random image generated on an iPad, and the claim is that their nonverbal autistic child can then pick up what that image is without being shown it. Michels describes this in a conversation with the writer Whitley Strieber, drawing on The Telepathy Tapes, a podcast series made by the filmmaker Ky Dickens with the psychiatrist Diane Powell. If it holds, it would point to some kind of mind-to-mind communication."
